<section class="section wrap grid3">
  <article class="panel"><h3>Plan design support</h3><p>Translate your retirement objective into an understandable plan design conversation, with contribution targets and business realities in view.</p></article>
  <article class="panel"><h3>Documentation coordination</h3><p>Keep the plan documents, onboarding steps, and professional handoffs moving in the right order.</p></article>
  <article class="panel"><h3>Annual administration</h3><p>Coordinate census information, participant records, annual testing, reporting, and the details that keep a plan current.</p></article>
  <article class="panel"><h3>Compliance workflow</h3><p>Stay organized around deadlines, notices, required filings, and the professional certifications that belong in the process.</p></article>
</section>

<section class="section alt"><div class="wrap split">
  <div>
    <p class="kicker">What we take off your plate</p>
    <h2>A more connected way to manage a complex plan.</h2>
    <p>The strongest plan strategy can lose momentum when the annual work is fragmented. Our role is to make the handoffs clear, the documentation organized, and the path forward easier to see.</p>
    <p>Design without a census is a sketch. Administration without a calendar is a scramble in July. Sterling sits between the owner, the CPA, and the independent Enrolled Actuary so those three are not discovering the same fact in three different months. The recurring work is described on <a href="/administration">administration</a>. The annual review list is on <a href="/compliance">compliance</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <img class="photo" src="/images/admin.jpg" alt="Illustration representing pension compliance and TPA governance" style="height:380px;" />
</div></section>

<section class="section wrap">
  <p class="kicker">How we partner</p>
  <h2>Built to keep owners, advisors, and administrators aligned.</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A dedicated point of contact who knows the history of your plan</li>
    <li>Clear, plain-English communication at each meaningful milestone</li>
    <li>Thoughtful coordination with CPAs, attorneys, investment professionals, and independent Enrolled Actuaries</li>
    <li>A long-term view of the plan—not just a transaction at the end of the year</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We are not the actuary, the CPA, the attorney, or the investment adviser. When the filing needs a certified valuation, that signature belongs to an independent Enrolled Actuary. When the return needs a deduction, that signature belongs to your CPA. Sterling’s job is the plan’s administration and the coordination around it. The fee split is on <a href="/fees">fees and who does what</a>.</p>
</section>

<section class="section wrap"><div class="cta">
  <div><p class="kicker">Need a steadier process?</p><h2>Bring us the complicated version.</h2><p>We’ll help you sort through what’s in place, what’s missing, and which next step matters most.</p></div>
  <a class="btn gold" href="/contact">Set up a consultation</a>
</div></section>

